<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Holstein</h1><p class="st-meta">1111 CE – 1474 CE · capital Rendsburg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A north German county between the Elbe and the Eider, ruled by the Schauenburg counts, whose union with Schleswig shaped centuries of Danish-German history.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1111 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-iii-holy-roman-emperor">Duke Lothair of Saxony</a> granted the County of Holstein and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stormarn">Stormarn</a> to Adolf I of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-schaumburg">Schauenburg</a>. His successors pushed into Slavic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wagria">Wagria</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-ii-of-holstein">Adolf II</a> founded <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-and-hanseatic-city-of-lubeck">Lübeck</a> in 1143. Holstein was lost to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> in 1201 but regained after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bornhoved">Battle of Bornhöved</a> in 1227.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The county repeatedly divided into lines such as Holstein-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiel">Kiel</a>, Holstein-Plön and Holstein-Rendsburg. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gerhard-iii-count-of-holstein-rendsburg">Gerhard III the Great of Holstein-Rendsburg</a> dominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> in the 1330s, ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jutland">Jutland</a> until his murder in 1340. Holstein's counts gained the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-schleswig">Duchy of Schleswig</a> in 1386, binding the two lands together.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Rendsburg line died out in 1459, and the estates of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a> and Holstein chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-i-of-denmark">King Christian I of Denmark</a> as ruler in 1460 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-ribe">Treaty of Ribe</a>. In 1474 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-holy-roman-emperor">Emperor Frederick III</a> raised Holstein to a duchy. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/provisional-government-of-schleswig-holstein">Schleswig-Holstein</a> Question later troubled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> until 1864.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/county-of-holstein.jpg" alt="County of Holstein" width="320" height="384"><figcaption>Image: Ipankonin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Holstein_Arms.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1111 CE – 1474 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rendsburg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Adolf II of Holstein, Gerhard III of Holstein-Rendsburg</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Low German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Holstein, Holstein-Rendsburg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1292&amp;focus=county-of-holstein" aria-label="County of Holstein on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4894 320 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Holstein lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5214 576L5237 629M5214 576L5229 694M5214 576L5274 535M5214 576L5209 586M5214 576L5218 590"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5237 629h0M5229 694h0M5274 535h0M5209 586h0M5218 590h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5214 576h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5214 576h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1292&amp;focus=county-of-holstein">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
